src/jmath/trig.rs ports sin and cos as Android's libm (bionic) carries them:
FreeBSD msun's s_sin.c, s_cos.c, k_sin.c, k_cos.c and e_rem_pio2.c, which are
fdlibm 5.3's routines as FreeBSD revised them (e_rem_pio2.c optimized by
Bruce D. Evans) under the same Sun notice. It evaluates them as Android
builds them, with -ffp-contract=off, so no operation is fused.

The port is distributed under the repository's licence; its full text is
LICENSE at the root of this repository. The app lists material-color-utilities
and fdlibm among its third-party licences
(app/src/main/config/libraries/material-color-utilities.json and fdlibm.json);
MaterialKolor is listed from its Gradle dependency.
